## App-name: account
> Handles accounts management and authentications

* User Roles
    - See `auth/UserRole.py`
    - App Admin - `default django superuser`
    - Super Admin - `created from command line for specific tasks like school creation, etc.`
    - Admin - `School accounts`
    - Staff - `School staff accounts, has  subroles which can be created from superadmin`
    - Student - `School student accounts, created from mobile app only`

* Models
    - Account - `models.py`
    - AuthToken- `auth/AuthToken.py`

* Views
    - `auth/Authentication.py` - handles authentication, uses BaseTokenAuthentication.
    - `auth/context.py` - uses contextvars for client for every request.
    - `auth/OTP.py` - OTP services using `pyoyp`.

* Urls
    - /signin
    - /change_password
    - /profile
    - /account_update
    - /obtain - `validate token from cookie/header`
    - /superadmins
    - /\<role\>/register
    - /otp/verify
    - /otp/resend
    - /logout

* Note:
    - otp, sms_api, app_device_token, etc. stored in account.
    - Token obtained from cookie/header.

